# The Deal-to-Challenge Graph Engine needs no environment variables.
#
# Everything runs locally: ingestion, normalisation, decomposition, the
# operating-model classifier, the DAG engine, the quality gate and the exports are
# deterministic TypeScript with zero runtime dependencies, and the AI layer runs
# in mock mode (`MockProvider`) with no network access at all.
#
# Copying this file is therefore optional; it exists so the absence of a real
# `.env` is explicit rather than an oversight.
#
# If you later add a live AI provider, keep its key out of source control: put it
# in `.env.local` (already gitignored) and read it through `import.meta.env`,
# never as a literal in a committed file.
#
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
